abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 formalization, over Mathlib, of the results of
  "The quantum query complexity of the semigroup product problem" by Troy Lee
  and Miklos Santha. The problem is to compute a product x_1 ... x_n in a
  fixed finite semigroup when one query reveals one input element. For
  nontrivial finite commutative aperiodic monoids the bounded-error quantum
  query complexity is Theta(min{n, sqrt(n beta)}), where the product breadth
  beta bounds the length of a product-preserving subsequence. The library also
  covers monoids with a stable partial order whose minimum is the identity,
  and arbitrary finite aperiodic semigroups. It builds on the
  QuantumQueryComplexity library and the Rao-BCW sunflower bound.
